      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name means ‘White Ovre’, named after the white‑chalk church that stood there, contrasting with Rødovre’s red brick.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
